course: dictionary
lesson: 932
title: Blindly: without looking or without thinking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Blindly comes from the word blind, and it has two meanings. The first is without looking, or without being able to see. «The Mole panics, runs blindly, falls over things» means he runs without seeing where he is going.
explain: The second meaning is without thinking first, or without asking questions. «Robots follow instructions blindly unless they use sensors to check the world» means a robot does what it is told, even when it is wrong, unless it checks first.
explain: To work out which meaning fits, ask: is someone acting without seeing, or without thinking? Then put your meaning into the sentence and see whether it still makes sense.
fact: Blindly means without looking, or without being able to see.
fact: Blindly also means without thinking first, or without asking questions.
fact: Blindly is an adverb, made from the adjective blind.
fact: «Picking blindly from a bag» means picking something without looking into the bag.
fact: Do not blindly trust a stranger or a website: check first.
exercise: «Robots follow instructions blindly unless they use sensors.» What does blindly mean here? | Only when they are asked nicely | *Without checking first | Slowly and carefully | Very quickly and happily
exercise: «The Mole panics, runs blindly, and falls over things.» What does blindly mean in this sentence? | Back to his home | *Without being able to see where he is going | Happily, with a song | Slowly and carefully, step by step
exercise: Which sentence shows someone acting blindly in the second sense? | A girl reads the map carefully before she sets off | *A girl copies a stranger's plan blindly, without asking a single question | A boy checks the water with his hand | A girl asks her teacher to explain the rule
test: Ben picks one card blindly from a pile. What does he do? | He reads every card before choosing | He throws the whole pile away | *He chooses one without looking at the cards | He asks his friend to choose for him
test: A new app asks you to share your password. Why should you not blindly agree? | Because the app is always right | *Because you should check first that it is safe | Because blindly means you must agree quickly | Because passwords are boring
exam: On a rocky desert path, what could running blindly lead to? | A rest | A song | A picnic | *A fall
